      "fieldname": "col_merge_prevention",
      "fieldtype": "Column Break",
      "label": "GL Merge Prevention"
    },
    {
      "fieldname": "merge_prevention_help",
      "fieldtype": "HTML",
      "options": "<div class=\"alert alert-info\" style=\"margin-top: 0.5rem\">\n<p>When <b>Prevent GL Entry Merging</b> is enabled:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Each Journal Entry Account row populates <code>reference_detail_no</code> before submit, giving it a unique merge key.</li>\n<li>GL Entries created from Journal Entries will carry the <code>letter</code> value from the corresponding JE Account row.</li>\n<li>Updates to letters on submitted Journal Entries are synced back to their GL Entries.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>When disabled, these hooks are bypassed and ERPNext\u2019s default GL merge behaviour applies.</p>\n</div>"
    },
    {
      "default": "0",
      "description": "When enabled, each JE Account row produces a separate GL Entry, preserving per-row letter distinctions.",
      "fieldname": "prevent_gl_merge",
      "fieldtype": "Check",
      "label": "Prevent GL Entry Merging"
    },
    {
      "fieldname": "col_rebuild_subset",
      "fieldtype": "Column Break",
      "label": "Historical Rebuild Scope"
    },
    {
      "fieldname": "subset_help",
      "fieldtype": "HTML",
      "options": "<div class=\"alert alert-info\" style=\"margin-top: 0.5rem\">\n<p>Select a <b>company</b> and either choose a <b>posting date range</b> or enable <b>Use Entire History</b>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Eligible</b> vouchers still have merged GL rows and can be rebuilt safely.</li>\n<li><b>Blocked</b> vouchers need manual attention first, such as reopening the fiscal period or enabling Journal Entry reposting.</li>\n<li><b>Already Correct</b> vouchers do not need any rebuild.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The preview does not modify data.</p>\n</div>"
    },
    {
      "fieldname": "rebuild_company",
      "fieldtype": "Link",
      "label": "Company",
      "options": "Company"
    },
    {
      "default": "0",
